# Citation metadata. GitHub renders this as the repository's "Cite this
# repository" button. There is no paper behind tddlog yet, so this
# describes the software itself; `preferred-citation` redirects citations
# to one once it is written.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tddlog: ProbLog inference by Tp-compilation into Tree Decision Diagrams"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Van den Broeck"
    given-names: "Guy"
    affiliation: "Computer Science Department, University of California, Los Angeles"
abstract: >-
  Exact marginal probabilities for probabilistic logic programs in the
  Datalog fragment of ProbLog, and for Bayesian and Markov networks
  written as programs. The program is compiled by Tp-compilation into
  tree decision diagrams with the tididi library, and the queries are
  counted on the diagrams.
keywords:
  - probabilistic logic programming
  - ProbLog
  - knowledge compilation
  - decision diagram
  - weighted model counting
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tractables/tddlog"
url: "https://tractables.github.io/tddlog/"
version: 0.1.0
